  <h2>What shoppers actually browse</h2>
  <h3>Luxury evening (Chanel, Louis Vuitton, Burberry)</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Chanel</strong>, <strong>Louis Vuitton</strong>, and <strong>Burberry</strong> formal rows emphasise logo placement, lining quality, and zipper stacks.
    QC focus: bust dart symmetry, hem circumference, interior label fonts.
  </p>
  <h3>Streetwear crossovers (BAPE, Jordan, Adidas)</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>A Bathing Ape</strong>, <strong>Jordan</strong>, and <strong>Adidas</strong> dress listings mix sportswear branding with formal silhouettes—confirm you want the hybrid look before paste.
  </p>

  <h2>QC checklist for formal dress rows</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Length &amp; fit:</strong> flat measurements bust, waist, hip, shoulder-to-hem.</li>
    <li><strong>Lining:</strong> colour match, seam finish, no visible puckering.</li>
    <li><strong>Zipper &amp; closures:</strong> branded pulls, snag-free operation in video QC.</li>
    <li><strong>Embroidery / logos:</strong> alignment on curved panels—<a href="/blog/kakobuy-4k-qc-video-inspection-guide/">4K video</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Size tags:</strong> confirm EU/US/Asian sizing before export approval.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Pair with <a href="/blog/kakobuy-sizing-spreadsheet-apparel/">apparel sizing notes</a>—formal cuts punish vanity sizing drift.
  </p>

  <h2>Freight &amp; timing notes</h2>
  <p>
    Dresses ship lighter than coats but may need garment bags or stiff packaging that adds DIM weight.
    Event buyers should pad timelines with warehouse storage limits—<a href="/blog/kakobuy-warehouse-storage-spreadsheet/">storage policy</a>—and honest customs buffers for international lanes.
  </p>

